---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout
  title={`${site.city} Water Quality Report`}
  description={`Where ${site.city}, ${site.stateAbbr} tap water comes from, who manages it, and how hard it is by ZIP code.`}
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Water Quality" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Local Water Data</p>
      <h1>{site.city} Water Quality & Hardness Report</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-header-image-section">
    <div class="container">
      <img src="/water-quality-header.webp" alt={`Testing tap water hardness in ${site.city}, ${site.stateAbbr}`} class="page-header-image" width="1600" height="500" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="brand-backlink">
        <a href="/" class="brand-link">{site.businessName}</a>
        {" "}provides water hardness testing and quality reporting across {site.city} and {site.county}.
      </p>

      <div class="section-header">
        <p>{site.waterAuthority} sources {site.city}'s public water supply from {site.waterSource}. Homes across {site.county} see hardness levels of {site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} grains per gallon (GPG), classified as {site.gpgLabel} — see the ZIP-by-ZIP breakdown below.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Water Source</h3>
          <p>{site.city} draws its supply from {site.waterSource}, unlike cities that rely solely on groundwater wells.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Managing Authority</h3>
          <p>{site.waterAuthority} treats and distributes this supply to every {site.city} address.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Understanding {site.gpgLabel} Water</h2>
        <p>Water hardness is measured in grains per gallon (GPG) of dissolved calcium and magnesium. {site.city}'s {site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} GPG range falls in the "{site.gpgLabel}" category on the five-tier scale below, per the Water Quality Association:</p>
      </div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>GPG Range</th><th>Classification</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>0 – 1</td><td>Soft</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1 – 3.5</td><td>Slightly Hard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3.5 – 7</td><td>Moderately Hard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>7 – 10.5</td><td>Hard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10.5+</td><td>Very Hard</td></tr>
          <tr class="highlight"><td>{site.gpgLow} – {site.gpgHigh}</td><td>{site.city}, {site.stateAbbr} ({site.gpgLabel})</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Hardness by ZIP Code</h2>
        <p>Hardness readings can vary slightly by neighbourhood and distribution line, so here are approximate figures for {site.zipCodes.length} {site.city} ZIP codes:</p>
      </div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>ZIP Code</th><th>Approx. Hardness</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.zipCodes.map((zip) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{zip}</td>
              <td>{site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} GPG ({site.gpgLabel})</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>A salt-based softener is the only system type that fully removes hardness minerals at these readings — see how it compares to salt-free conditioning on our <a href="/comparison/">system comparison page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container final-cta">
      <h2>Get Your Exact Hardness Reading</h2>
      <p>As of the most recent {site.waterAuthority} reporting period, book a <a href="/free-water-test/">free in-home water test</a> to know exactly what {site.city} water is doing to your plumbing.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote/">Get a Free Water Softener Quote in {site.city}</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .highlight td { background: var(--color-primary-light); color: var(--color-primary-dark); font-weight: 700; }
    .final-cta { text-align: center; }
    .final-cta p { max-width: 48ch; margin: 0 auto 24px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
